-- Tax paid over: a challan can pay the tax withheld on an expense and the salary tax of a payroll run.
-- track: C
--
-- The CREATE TABLE / index statements are generated by drizzle-kit from
-- src/modules/tax-paid-over/schema.ts. The sections marked "hand-written" are not managed by
-- Drizzle. Reverse with the file of the same name in drizzle/down.
--
-- Why: a challan (Step 26, drizzle/0032_supplier_payments.sql) records tax paid to the
-- government, and pays the tax withheld on supplier bills: its rows point at a bill's
-- withholding entry. Two later steps of this track credit the same accounts with tax no
-- challan could pay: tax withheld on an expense (Step 34, expense_withholdings) and the income
-- tax a payroll run deducts from pay under section 149 (Step 41, payroll_runs.tax). Both stayed
-- "still to be paid" for good and the account in the books only grew.
--
-- What this adds, beside what is there and changing none of it:
--
--   1. challan_expense_entries and challan_payroll_runs: which expense's tax and which payroll
--      run's tax a challan paid. Each once, whole. Written only by the function below; never
--      changed or removed. Read by the owner, an accountant and the auditor: an expense's row by
--      whoever may read that expense, a payroll run's row only by someone who works in every
--      branch, as payroll itself is read.
--
--   2. app.record_tax_challan: one challan that pays any mix of tax withheld on bills, tax
--      withheld on expenses, and (for income tax) the salary tax of approved payroll runs. It
--      is the challan of Step 26 in every way: the same table, a WC- number from
--      number_series, the same journal (debit the withholding payable account of its kind,
--      credit the cash or bank account), the same audit rows, the same roles. For bills' entries
--      it asks exactly what app.record_withholding_challan asks; that function is left as it
--      is and still records a challan that pays bills' entries only.
--
--   3. An expense whose withheld tax has been paid over is no longer cancelled: the tax is
--      with the government in the supplier's name, and a reversal would take it back out of
--      the books as if it had never been paid.
--
-- No row of any company changes. No amount or rate is typed: a challan's amount is the sum of
-- the rows it pays.
--
-- Database error codes (the money range, SE300 to SE399):
--   SE379  a challan is of one kind of tax, has a number, and pays whole amounts withheld or
--          deducted on or before its date, each once; salary tax is income tax
--   SE380  tax withheld on this expense has been paid over, so the expense stands

CREATE TABLE "challan_expense_entries" (
	"tenant_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"challan_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"entry_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "challan_expense_entries_entry_key" UNIQUE("tenant_id","entry_id")
);
--> statement-breakpoint
CREATE TABLE "challan_payroll_runs" (
	"tenant_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"challan_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"run_id" uuid NOT NULL,
	"amount" numeric(20, 2) NOT NULL,
	CONSTRAINT "challan_payroll_runs_run_key" UNIQUE("tenant_id","run_id")
);
--> statement-breakpoint
